<title>SOUTH KOREA: Kyungki Bank warned for improper loans.</title>
<headline>Kyungki Bank warned for improper loans.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office of Bank Supervision said on Thursday it had warned the regional Kyungki Bank for improper loan procedures involving about two billion won.</p>
<p>The office said in a statement that the bank was found to have extended 700 million won to a company which used a borrowed name bank account, an illegal practice.</p>
<p>The bank also supplied 1.1 billion won to a company with poor financial status and discounted notes worth 225 million won without checking financial conditions of the issuer.</p>
</text>
